-\paragraph{Results in brief.} Q1: pooled over the six fresh markets and without honest churn, R3 and C$^*$ are ``\site{int_q1_cat}'' within the registered margin under X7-SC and under D2+H3 (Section~\ref{sec:results}). Q4: the registered B3--R3 gain-and-efficiency comparison passes on \site{int_q4_k} of six fresh markets, all three passes qualified by search flags. Q2 and Q3 (Appendix~\ref{sec:app-results}): the priority phase and newest-first targeting each lower the measured gain (main effects \site{int_q2_p} and \site{int_q2_g}), and either one alone accounts for most of the reduction; the selected unconstrained welfare attack lowers R3's gross efficiency to \site{int_q3_w0}, and the registered W1 search (efficiency \site{int_w1}) supplies no efficiency bound for randomised attacks. The two follow-ups are in Sections~\ref{sec:reset} and~\ref{sec:churn}; the end of Section~\ref{sec:churn} reports the prospective replication on new markets.
+\paragraph{Results in brief.} Q1: pooled over the six fresh markets and without honest churn, R3 and C$^*$ are ``\site{int_q1_cat}'' within the registered margin under X7-SC and under D2+H3 (Section~\ref{sec:results}). Q4: the registered B3--R3 gain-and-efficiency comparison passes on \site{int_q4_k} of six fresh markets, all three passes qualified by search flags. Q2 and Q3 (Appendix~\ref{sec:app-results}): the priority phase and newest-first targeting each lower the measured gain (main effects \site{int_q2_p} and \site{int_q2_g}), and either one alone accounts for most of the reduction; the selected unconstrained welfare attack lowers R3's gross efficiency to \site{int_q3_w0}, and the registered W1 search (efficiency \site{int_w1}) supplies no efficiency bound for randomised attacks. The two follow-ups are in Sections~\ref{sec:reset} and~\ref{sec:churn}; the end of Section~\ref{sec:churn} reports the prospective-exploratory replication on new markets.
